  "notes": [
    "Go 1.26 new permits exactly one type or value expression; make retains its existing typed argument list.",
    "The type alternative dynamic precedence compensates the upstream type-identifier precedence so existing new(any) and new(int) retain their type-node reading.",
    "Go 1.27 concrete methods reuse function declarations type-parameter syntax; interface methods remain unchanged.",
    "Empty statements consume their own semicolon; terminated ordinary statements and a final unterminated statement preserve separators without requiring a second semicolon after an empty statement. Empty labeled statements retain the upstream labeled_statement alias and declared ambiguity."
  ]
